Q8. Write a short note on: Responsibility of holding company for preparation of CFS.
The responsibility for preparation & presentation of CFS, is of the mngt of parent. This includes:
(i) Identifying components, and including the financial information of the components to be
included in the consolidated financial statements;
(ii) Obtaining accurate and complete financial information from components;
(iii) Identifying related parties and related party transactions for reporting;
(iv) Where appropriate, identifying reportable segments for segmental reporting;
(v) Making appropriate consolidation adjustments;
(vi) Harmonization of accounting policies and accounting framework; and
(vii) GAAP conversion, where applicable

Q9. Write short note on Auditor's objectives in an audit of CFS.
The auditor's objectives in an audit of consolidated financial statements are:
(i) The auditor should also validate the requirement of preparation of CFS for the company as
per applicable financial reporting framework.
(ii) To satisfy himself that the consolidated financial statements have been prepared in
accordance with the requirements of applicable financial reporting framework;
(iii) to enable himself to express opinion on true and fair view presented by the CFS;
(iv) to enquire into the matters as specified in section 143(1) of the Companies Act, 2013;
